@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/odp#>.

:Ontology a owl:Ontology ;
rdfs:label "Author Name Ontology" ;
rdfs:comment "An ontology for modeling author names and name changes.".

:Author a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Author" ;
rdfs:comment "An author who writes books.".

:Name a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Name" ;
rdfs:comment "A name adopted by an author.".

:AdoptedName a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Adopted Name" ;
rdfs:comment "A name adopted by an author for a specific book.".

:Book a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Book" ;
rdfs:comment "A book written by an author.".

:AuthorName a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Author Name" ;
rdfs:comment "A name used by an author for a specific book.".

:nameChange a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Name Change" ;
rdfs:comment "A change of name adopted by an author.".

:marriage a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Marriage" ;
rdfs:comment "A marriage that results in a name change for an author.".

:Author rdfs:subClassOf :Person.
:Person a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Person" ;
rdfs:comment "A person who may adopt different names.".

:Name rdfs:subClassOf :String.
:AdoptedName rdfs:subClassOf :Name.
:AuthorName rdfs:subClassOf :Name.
:Book rdfs:subClassOf :Publication.
:Publication a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Publication" ;
rdfs:comment "A publication written by an author.".

:nameChange rdfs:subClassOf :Change.
:Change a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Change" ;
rdfs:comment "A change of name or other attribute.".

:marriage rdfs:subClassOf :NameChange.

:Author rdfs:hasName :Name.
:Author rdfs:hasAdoptedName :AdoptedName.
:AdoptedName rdfs:hasAuthor :Author.
:Book rdfs:hasAuthor :Author.
:Author rdfs:hasBook :Book.
:Name rdfs:hasAuthor :Author.
:AuthorName rdfs:hasAuthor :Author.
:Author rdfs:hasNameChange :NameChange.
:NameChange rdfs:hasOldName :Name.
:NameChange rdfs:hasNewName :Name.
:marriage rdfs:hasNameChange :NameChange.

Intent:
This ontology models the relationship between an author and their adopted names, including name changes due to marriage.

Covered requirements:

* An author can adopt different names for different books.
* An author can change their name due to marriage.
* A book can have only one author.
* An author can have multiple books.
* A name can be adopted by only one author.
* A name change can be due to marriage.

Known assumptions and exclusions:

* This ontology assumes that an author's name is a string.
* This ontology does not model the relationship between an author and their books beyond the fact that an author can have multiple books.
* This ontology does not model the relationship between an author and their personal information beyond their name and marriage status.